%H A402357 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A399885/a399885.py.txt">Python program (unlabeled_reducible_elections.py)</a>, Nov 2026.
%F A402357 Let A(0)=1, B=x*A and A=MSET(SEQ_{>=1}(B)). Then the ordinary generating function U(x)=Sum_{n>=1} a(n)x^n is CYC(B)-B*SEQ_{>=1}(B), by block-tree dissymmetry.  In ordinary series, SEQ_{>=1}(F)=F/(1-F), MSET(F)=exp(Sum_{k>=1}F(x^k)/k) and CYC(F)=Sum_{k>=1}phi(k)/k*log(1/(1-F(x^k))), where phi is Euler's totient function.
%o A402357 (Python)
